  "deathBeat": [
   "d40: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Theo Menon is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
   "d40: 🕯️ Theo Menon is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
   "d40: The village's quarrel was with Theo — and Theo is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers."
  ],
  "recoverHome": [
   "d41: That night, they bring Theo home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours."
  ],
  "vouch": [
   "d40: At the grave, Declan, Ruth, Ole and 2 more speak for Michael — \"Theo trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens."
  ],
  "systemVoice": [
   "d40: SYSTEM: \"Perimeter violated! This is unprecedented! ...Is this unprecedented? Checking. Yes. Unprecedented.\"",
   "d40: SYSTEM: You know this plant the way it knows itself. Concerning. Impressive."
  ],
  "burialWindowSay": [
   "d40: The village's quarrel was with Theo — and Theo is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
   "d40: At the grave, Declan, Ruth, Ole and 2 more speak for Michael — \"Theo trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
   "d40: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+2 integration)",
   "d40: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+2 integration)",
   "d41: That night, they bring Theo home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours.",
