 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_tjssx2a",
   "entryDay": 40,
   "cause": "the expedition",
   "lines": [
    "d40: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Theo Menon is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d40: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d40: 🕯️ Theo Menon is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d40: What Theo kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d40: \"Theo's gone.\" Ole looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Theo.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d40: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Michael blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d40: 📖 LEARNED: Camp Cooking (Level 1). Cooking uses half the water, +10% kcal. Once per day: add a Secret Ingredient (a random inventory item) — 50% delicious (+morale), 50% educational.",
    "d40: 📖 LEARNED: Food Preservation (Level 1). Salt, smoke, dry. The big three. Salt draws water out; bacteria can't live without it.",
    "d40: 📖 LEARNED: Wound Care (Level 1). Clean it, close it, cover it. Pressure stops bleeding. Clean water is better than dirty hands.",
    "d40: ⚡ TECHNIQUE UNLOCKED: Precise Mend! Your healing knows where to go. +50% effectiveness. (Your knowledge of Wound Care amplifies your field_medicine.)",
    "d40: 📖 LEARNED: The Forager’s Eye (Level 1). You walk slower and see more. Food was always there; now you notice it.",
    "d40: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d40: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Theo Menon, 40 days. The mantle passes to Michael Joshi.",
    "d40: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Michael Joshi, 28 — a Baker. His hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Beard Moss, Green Thumb, Literally.",
    "d40: ◈ The System updates its file: the new bearer <redacted> \"Gardener of the Living Garden.\" It had a word for this one before the Codex came.",
    "d40: The village's quarrel was with Theo — and Theo is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d40: At the grave, Declan, Ruth, Ole and 2 more speak for Michael — \"Theo trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d40: The fire knew Michael before the Codex did — his name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_8dagxpd",
   "entryDay": 71,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d71: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Michael Joshi is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d71: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d71: Michael is gone — dead. The errand dies with them; nobody's waiting on those dandelions now.",
    "d71: 🕯️ Michael Joshi is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d71: What Michael kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d71: \"Michael's gone.\" Ole looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Michael.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d71: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Ruth blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d71: 📖 LEARNED: Wiring & Circuits (Level 1). Volts, amps, and why you respect both. Safe splices, real grounds, no shortcuts.",
    "d71: 📖 LEARNED: Tireless Stride (Level 1). You walk like water downhill — no wasted steps, no wasted breath. Every mile costs 15% less.",
    "d71: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d71: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Michael Joshi, 71 days. The mantle passes to Ruth Freeman.",
    "d71: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Ruth Freeman, 62 — an appliance repair tech. Her hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Echo Location.",
    "d71: The village's quarrel was with Michael — and Michael is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d71: You knew Michael — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting him, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d71: At the grave, Declan, Ole, Desmond and 4 more speak for Ruth — \"Michael trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d71: The fire knew Ruth before the Codex did — her name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
